    "sourceNotes": "From the national pilgrim office's 2024 statistics report, table of long-distance walkers by route on arrival at Nidaros Pilegrimsgård. The office counts the Gudbrandsdalsleden as one route, so these figures include walkers on both of its branches between Oslo and Lillehammer, of which this section is the western one. Not every pilgrim calls at the reception, and those who walk part of the route and do not reach Trondheim are not counted, so the true number of walkers is higher. See docs/data-sources.md."
